# 13. ACCESSIBILITY

Use WCAG 2.2 AA as the target.

At minimum:

- Normal text contrast should generally meet 4.5:1.
- Large text should meet the appropriate contrast threshold.
- Controls should have sufficient contrast.
- Focus indicators must be visible.
- Keyboard navigation must work.
- Forms must have labels.
- Errors must be understandable.
- Semantic headings must be logical.
- Images must have appropriate alternative text.
- Status must not be conveyed through colour alone.
- Interactive targets should generally be at least 44px where practical.
- Persistent actions must not obscure content.
- Screen-reader behaviour must be considered.

Previous design audits identified these specific issues:

- Muted progress text on ivory: approximately 2.84:1 contrast.
- Empty-field placeholder text on white: approximately 1.83:1.
- Copper placeholder-preview text: approximately 2.92:1.
- Some mobile filter/sort controls: 39px high.
- A menu control: 36px high.

Treat these as issues requiring verification and correction.

Do not recolour disabled controls indiscriminately. Assess their intended state and contrast separately.

Do not claim accessibility compliance without testing.

