# 15. VISUAL DESIGN QUALITY

The design should be premium and distinctive.

Use:
- Strong typography.
- Intentional whitespace.
- Clear hierarchy.
- Restrained colour.
- Thoughtful composition.
- Consistent grids.
- Appropriate visual emphasis.
- Purposeful imagery.
- Subtle motion.
- Well-crafted interface details.

Avoid making all sections look like identical card grids.

Use different layouts when the content requires them.

The public homepage, job discovery pages, worker profiles, employer dashboards and admin console should feel like related parts of one product, not identical templates.

Do not overdecorate.

Do not add unnecessary visual effects to compensate for weak information architecture.

Do not use imagery that creates a false impression of actual Tourms operations.

